# Audit trail

Source: [docs/audit-trail.md](../../docs/audit-trail.md). Cite it instead of
pasting the full architecture.

- Do not treat Better Auth `AuditLog`, upload audit rows, or `CatalogChangeLog`
  as the universal table-change audit trail. They are narrower logs.
- For broad table-change history, use Postgres row triggers plus
  transaction-local Prisma context (`set_config(..., true)`) so pooled
  connections do not leak actor data.
- Preserve impersonation accountability: record the real admin/operator as the
  actual actor and the impersonated user as the effective/acting-as user. Never
  attribute an impersonated write only to the impersonated account.
- Prefer full `old_values` / `new_values` JSONB snapshots plus
  `changed_fields` for audited tables unless volume data proves deltas are
  necessary.
- Keep UI metadata columns (`createdByUserId`, `updatedByUserId`, `createdAt`,
  `updatedAt`) when pages need fast creator/last-editor display; audit logs are
  for history and forensics.
- When adding audited mutations, route Server Actions, Route Handlers, and
  workers through the shared audit context helper instead of manual ad-hoc
  `log...()` calls.
